    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d152">

                <pb facs="0283" n="251" sameAs="frus:frus1958-60v06/pg251"/>

                <head>152. Telegram From the Embassy in Cuba to the Department of State<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d152-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Havana</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1958-11-04T17:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">November 4,
                                1958—5 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>466. It is essential in my judgment, for sound US policy determination re Cuba,
                    that our Government learn beyond any doubt whether and to what extent Castro
                    movement is penetrated, supported, influenced or directed by international
                    Communism. Our information on this subject to date is dangerously
                    inconclusive.</p>
                <p>[<hi rendition="#italic">2 paragraphs (6 lines) not declassified</hi>]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold">Smith</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
